from release_tools import package
package('V1.14.A2','''# V1.14.A2 — Clearer KPI Report Summaries

Amends V1.14.A1 with the requested KPI report display changes. The main KPI Records table replaces the average Store % display with Worst Store %: the available individual store deviation with the largest absolute magnitude, retaining its positive or negative sign. The cell identifies the store and shows flagged stores / total compared stores. Unavailable store percentages are counted and shown separately, including zero-baseline stores, so a known percentage cannot hide unavailable comparisons. Equal-magnitude ties use the existing saved store order. If no percentage is available, the cell says Unavailable. Missing KPI snapshots do not invent percentages or flagged-store counts.

A Review Reason column presents the saved KPI findings as Store sales, Retailer sales, Row count, Insufficient history or KPI fields. Multiple causes are shown together, repeated categories are collapsed, and unfamiliar historical messages retain an Other KPI check label rather than guessing their meaning. Reviewed and approved records retain their original reasons; cancelled records describe the results as a KPI snapshot instead of requesting approval. The details popup also shows the worst store, counts and reason summary, alongside the existing original messages and per-store comparisons.

These are read-only summaries of saved results, including historical runs. The original store mean remains stored. KPI calculations, thresholds, baseline eligibility, any-store flagging, job status, review requirements and approval behavior are unchanged. Both existing light and dark themes remain included.

The single outputs/V1.3.A1.bat launcher opens V1.14.A2 at http://127.0.0.1:5001/. Close the old server window and reopen the same batch file. Local data is preserved by SQLite backup. Databases, uploads, samples, secrets, personal configuration, installed dependencies and generated builds remain excluded from GitHub.
''','''Production Vite build passed. The committed frontend report summary test verifies balanced +50/-50 changes with a zero saved mean, larger negative changes, deterministic ties, flagged counts, unavailable percentages, all reason categories, category deduplication, unknown historical findings, healthy/missing results and snapshot immutability. Run node test/kpiReportSummary.test.js or npm run test:kpi-report from frontend-github. Ten existing KPI backend tests passed, covering comparisons, status, manual review and approval. Eight API/served-frontend regression tests passed. Interactive browser verification was not performed.
''',launcher=True)
